abstract:
Passive in situ remediation technologies (PIRT) use a variety of physical, chemical, or biological processes that act without significant human intervention in the subsurface to reduce the mass, toxicity, mobility, volume, or concentration of contaminants in soil or groundwater. Passive remediation uses the natural movement of water to disperse treatment chemicals or to move contaminated groundwater through a treatment zone. 


